From 52223b78ea9ab137398cb00b7ec5bca85aa32bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 20:57:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/38] feat(omni-tts): 9-row CustomVoice language conditioning
 (re-port 12ee383)

Port the CustomVoice language-conditioned Talker prefill onto the v0.9.0
runtime:

- TalkerGenerationRequest gains an optional `language` field; TalkerConfig
  gains codecThinkId + a codecLanguageId map read from optional config.json
  keys codec_think_id / codec_language_id.
- prepareTalkerInput lower-cases and resolves language -> langId (unknown or
  empty -> -1).
- projectToTalkerInput computes kFixedPrefixLen = (langId>=0) ? 9 : 8 and
  threads langId to the preamble kernel.
- talkerMLPKernels: assistantPreambleKernel/invokeAssistantPreamble gain
  codecThinkId + langId; langId >= 0 selects the 9-row prefix (codecThinkId
  at row 3, langId embed injected at row 5, remaining rows shifted by one).
  Last-text-row codec_bos marker kept on both paths (load-bearing, validated
  on the v0.8.0 branch).
- Omni segment path (buildTalkerPrefillFromSegments) passes langId=-1,
  matching the v0.8.0 branch (language not propagated there).

Opt-in: no `language` field / no config keys => langId=-1 => the 8-row
upstream layout, byte-identical behavior.

